{
  "title": "Cerumen as a Biomatrix for Canine Lymphoma Screening - Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center",
  "text": "Cerumen as a Biomatrix for Canine Lymphoma Screening - Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center\nSkip To Main Content\nCollege of Veterinary Medicine\nLloyd Veterinary Medical Center\nISU CVM\nNews\nCVM Directory\nContacts\nGive Now\nSign Ons\nSearch\nClose Search\nSearch\nSubmit Search\nReferring DVM Login\nToggle Menu\nLloyd Veterinary Medical Center\nClients\nEmergency Services\nMap & Directions\nMake an Appointment\nWhat to Expect\nPayment Policies\nDiscount for ISU Employees, Students and Working Dogs\nGiving\nDr. W. Eugene and Linda Lloyd\nLVMC Client Newsletter\nSmall Animal\nPrimary Care\nSpecialty Care\nSupport Services\nEmergency Services\nStaff Directory\nClinical Trials Center\nHixson-Lied Small Animal Hospital Video\nLarge Animal\nFood Animal & Camelid\nVeterinary Field Services\nSupport Services\nStaff Directory\nEquine\nEquine Field Services\nEquine Internal Medicine\nEquine Intensive Care Unit & Neonatal Intensive Care Unit\nEquine Surgery\nEquine Reproduction\nFarrier\nStaff Directory\nServices\nBlood Donor Program\nInfectious Disease Information\nSupport Services\nVeterinarians\nContact Us\nReferrals\nConsultations\nFollow-up on Mutual Patient\nElectronic Medical Records\nServices\nSurgical Suites Virtual Tour\nVet Pulse\nSmall Animal Directory\nLarge Animal Directory\nReferring DVM Portal Webinars\nContinuing Education\nClinical Trials\nEmployment\nCurrent Openings\nVet Tech & Animal Caretakers Openings\nInternships & Residencies\nISU CVM\nNews\nCVM Directory\nContacts\nGive Now\nSearch\nSubmit Search\nHome\nClinical Trials\n»\nCerumen as a Biomatrix for Canine Lymphoma Screening\nCerumen as a Biomatrix for Canine Lymphoma Screening\nEvaluate the cerumen biomatrix difference between healthy dogs and those diagnosed with multicentric lymphoma\nSpecies\nDogs\nArea of Study\nOncology\nPurpose of Study\nThe purpose of this study is to valuate the cerumen biomatrix difference between healthy dogs and those diagnosed with multicentric lymphoma using headspace gas chromatography-mass spectrometry.\nEligibility\nEligibility criteria are organized into two cohorts.\nHealthy dogs\nmust have an unremarkable physical examination with no evidence of otitis and normal CBC, chemistry panel, and, when available, urinalysis. All screening diagnostics for healthy controls are covered by the study. Dogs with\nlymphoma\nmust have a cytologic or histologic diagnosis of multicentric lymphoma and no evidence of ear infection on physical examination.\nOnce a dog is confirmed as a healthy control or as a treatment-naïve lymphoma case, sterile ear swabs will be collected for sample acquisition.\nExclusion\nExclusion criteria include any serious systemic illness, concurrent malignancies other than lymphoma, lymphoma subtypes that are not multicentric, and any prior treatment with prednisone, chemotherapy, or immunotherapies.\nContact\nFor Further information about the study, contact Dr. Musser, Margaret (mmusser@iastate.edu)\nCerumen as Biomatris for Canine Lymphoma Screening\nFacebook - Small Animal Hospital\nFacebook - Large Animal Hospital\nClients\nSmall Animal\nLarge Animal\nEquine\nServices\nVeterinarians\nClinical Trials\nEmployment\nQuick Links\nISU CVM\nNews\nCVM Directory\nContacts\nGive Now\nLloyd Veterinary Medical Center\n1809 S Riverside Drive\nAmes, Iowa 50011-1134\nSmall Animal\n:\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t515-294-4900\nEquine and Farm Animal\n:\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t515-294-1500\nPrivacy Policy\nNon-discrimination Policy\nDigital Access and Accessibility\nConsumer Information\n© Iowa State University of Science and Technology\n\t\t\t\t2026",
